refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
inttidy_config_count tidytidy
Returns the number of errors encountered in the configuration of the specified tidy tidy.

  &reftitle.examples;



    tidy_config_count example


<?php
$html = '<p>test</I>';

// Invalid values in a configuration array throw a TypeError as of PHP 8.5.0,
// so the invalid value is read from a configuration file
$configFile = tempnam(sys_get_temp_dir(), 'tidy');
file_put_contents($configFile, "wrap: abc\n");

$tidy = tidy_parse_string($html, $configFile);

/* This outputs 1, because 'abc' isn't a valid wrap value */
echo tidy_config_count($tidy);

unlink($configFile);
?>


    &example.outputs.similar;


